1. Speech recognition model: granite-speech-5.0-470m-turboctc
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Name:       IBM Granite Speech 5.0 470M TurboCTC
Licence:    Apache-2.0 (section 8)
Copyright:  Copyright IBM Corp.
Upstream:   https://huggingface.co/ibm-granite/granite-speech-5.0-470m-turboctc
            at revision 91dcb0605daf65f88dbb04fef015c423241d941d
Export:     https://huggingface.co/gagni/granite-speech-5.0-470m-turboctc-onnx
            at revision 67e808153220ecd3d8614adab9379c0d17bbe024 (Apache-2.0)

The package carries a model derived from IBM's model in two steps. A community export by gagni
converted the upstream weights to ONNX with 8-bit integer quantisation of the matrix weights
(file model.int8.onnx; tokenizer.json is unchanged). This application then derives the graph it
loads, model.int8.scores.onnx, from that export by appending nodes that output the per-frame
peak probability of the recognition output; no weight is retrained or changed. The upstream and
export licences are Apache-2.0, and this notice states that the files were modified.

The export's own NOTICE file reads:

    granite-speech-5.0-470m-turboctc ONNX int8

    This is a derivative of ibm-granite/granite-speech-5.0-470m-turboctc
    (https://huggingface.co/ibm-granite/granite-speech-5.0-470m-turboctc,
    revision 91dcb0605daf65f88dbb04fef015c423241d941d), Copyright IBM Corp.,
    licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

    Modifications: the model was exported to ONNX with the feature extraction and
    the final argmax inside the graph, the block attention and subsampling were
    rewritten without shape branches (same computation), and the MatMul weights
    were quantized to int8. tokenizer.json is unchanged. The scripts in export/
    reproduce the files.

