3. Speaker embedding model: wespeaker-campplus-lm
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Name:       WeSpeaker CAM++ (VoxCeleb, large-margin fine-tuned)
Version:    wespeaker_en_voxceleb_CAM++_LM.onnx as distributed by k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx in the
            release "speaker-recongition-models" (the spelling is the release's own)
Licence:    Apache-2.0 for the code (section 8); CC-BY-4.0 for the weights
            (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)
Copyright:  Copyright the WeSpeaker authors
Source:     https://github.com/wenet-e2e/wespeaker
            https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx/releases/tag/speaker-recongition-models

Data note: the weights were trained on VoxCeleb, whose audio comes from public online videos.
WeSpeaker states that its pretrained models follow the licence of the dataset they were trained
on, and for VoxCeleb that is CC-BY-4.0
(https://github.com/wenet-e2e/wespeaker/blob/master/docs/pretrained.md). The model is used here
only to compare voices within one recording; it is not changed, and the application does not
identify a person. Attribution is given under CC-BY-4.0: the weights are credited to the
WeSpeaker authors and to the VoxCeleb dataset (University of Oxford, Visual Geometry Group).

